      {"t":"mc","q":"You work a lot. (to a friend) =","o":["Du arbeitest viel.","Du arbeitst viel.","Du arbeitet viel.","Du arbeiten viel."],"why":"arbeit- ends in t, so an e slips in: du arbeitest."},
      {"t":"order","p":"Lena works in Berlin.","a":["Lena","arbeitet","in","Berlin."],"x":["arbeiten"],"why":"Lena takes the er/sie/es form: arbeitet."},
      {"t":"order","p":"We live in Hamburg.","a":["Wir","wohnen","in","Hamburg."],"x":["wohnt"],"why":"The wir form ends in -en: wohnen."},
      {"t":"order","p":"You work a lot. (to friends)","a":["Ihr","arbeitet","viel."],"x":["arbeitest"],"why":"The ihr form ends in -t; after arbeit- an e slips in: arbeitet."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"Er __ in Hamburg.","p":"He lives in Hamburg.","a":["wohnt"],"o":["wohnen","wohnst","wohne"],"why":"The er form ends in -t: wohnt."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"Du __ viel.","p":"You work a lot. (to a friend)","a":["arbeitest"],"o":["arbeitst","arbeitet","arbeiten"],"why":"The du form ends in -st, and after arbeit- an e slips in: arbeitest."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"Ihr __ Tennis.","p":"You play tennis. (to friends)","a":["spielt"],"o":["spielen","spielst","spiele"],"why":"The ihr form ends in -t: spielt."},
      {"t":"type","p":"I'm learning German.","a":["Ich lerne Deutsch."],"hint":"lernen · Deutsch","x":["lernt","bin"],"why":"The ich form ends in -e: lerne. No form of sein is needed for -ing."},
      {"t":"type","p":"You work in Munich. (to a friend)","a":["Du arbeitest in München."],"hint":"arbeiten · München","x":["arbeitet"],"why":"The du form ends in -st, and after arbeit- an e slips in: arbeitest."},
      {"t":"type","p":"They play soccer.","a":["Sie spielen Fußball."],"hint":"spielen · der Fußball","x":["spielt"],"why":"Plural subject: the verb ending is -en, spielen."}
